<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Netherlands Antilles</h1><p class="st-meta">1954 CE – 2010 CE · capital Willemstad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Autonomous country of six Dutch Caribbean islands within the Kingdom of the Netherlands from 1954, dissolved into separate parts in 2010.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Charter for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a>, signed on 15 December 1954, turned the colony of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-curacao">Curaçao and Dependencies</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> Antilles, an equal partner with the Netherlands and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/suriname">Suriname</a>. It comprised <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/curacao">Curaçao</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aruba">Aruba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonaire">Bonaire</a> off <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/venezuela">Venezuela</a>, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sint-maarten">Sint Maarten</a>, Saba and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sint-eustatius">Sint Eustatius</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands">Leewards</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Antilles had their own parliament, the Staten, and government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/willemstad">Willemstad</a>, while the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> handled defence and foreign affairs. Oil refining on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/curacao">Curaçao</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aruba">Aruba</a>, offshore finance and tourism sustained the economy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papiamento">Papiamentu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and English were spoken. Labour unrest erupted in the Curaçao riots of 30 May 1969, which brought Afro-Curaçaoan politicians to power. Resentment of Curaçao's dominance grew on the smaller islands.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aruba">Aruba</a> left in 1986 to become a separate country. On 10 October 2010 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> Antilles were dissolved: <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/curacao">Curaçao</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sint-maarten">Sint Maarten</a> became countries within the kingdom, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonaire">Bonaire</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sint-eustatius">Sint Eustatius</a> and Saba became special municipalities of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/netherlands-antilles.jpg" alt="Netherlands Antilles" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Netherlands_Antilles_(1986%E2%80%932010).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1954 CE – 2010 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Willemstad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Papiamentu, Dutch and English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/curacao">Curaçao</a>, <a href="/countries/sint-maarten">Sint Maarten</a>, <a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dutch Antilles</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1982&amp;focus=netherlands-antilles" aria-label="Netherlands Antilles on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2786 1726 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Netherlands Antilles lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3106 1982L3106 1982M3106 1982L5110 626M3106 1982L3077 1967M3106 1982L3106 1982M3106 1982L3290 1765"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3106 1982h0M5110 626h0M3077 1967h0M3106 1982h0M3290 1765h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3106 1982h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3106 1982h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Willemstad. <a href="/atlas?year=1982&amp;focus=netherlands-antilles">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
